\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|work/o1/base2~}, \code{\verb~|tree2~}}\td{21:44:53Z}\td{E1's fix of E1-F1 .. F6 (21:26:43Z)}\td{\code{\verb~|5945b6568177~}}\td{\code{\verb~|aa1cd79a3f45~}}\td{\strong{every number below unless it says otherwise} (\code{\verb~|patches-main2127Z/~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|work/o1/base3~}, \code{\verb~|tree3~}}\td{22:42:39Z}\td{E1's \code{\verb~|eager~} (bit 26, 21:57:52Z) and \code{\verb~|convexpect~} (bit 27, 22:42:39Z)}\td{\code{\verb~|97d17e57e51b~}}\td{\code{\verb~|dc15612eb3f2~}}\td{the delivered patch (\code{\verb~|work/o1/patches/~}): rebased once more and checked, not timed}}
}

\p{With the switch off the patched jar is counter-identical to the published jar on all three trees (every \code{\verb~|machine.*~} statistic equal on two corpora each). The counts of the first tree are within 0.2 points of the second's (\code{\verb~|work/o1/counts/table.md~}).}

\p{X1's patch (\code{\verb~|0001-eval-visit-filter.main-1653Z.patch~}) applied to the tree of 21:08Z as it was. On top of it:}

\ol{
\li{\strong{A named switch}: \code{\verb~|once~} = \code{\verb~|Op.SW_ONCE~} (bit 27 on the tree of 21:27Z, bit 28 on the tree of 22:42Z), read and printed by \code{\verb~|Debug~}; not in \code{\verb~|all~}, not in \code{\verb~|Op.SW_DEFAULT~}, not in \code{\verb~|Op.SW_EXPERIMENTS~}: \code{\verb~|-X machine.switches=default,once~}. Off in strict mode (\code{\verb~|Eval.once(m)~}: \code{\verb~|!m.strict~}; a strict engine has no switch anyway) and under the debug modes that own the memo hit path (X1's rule). X1's measurement bit 128 of \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.m2.x~} is gone.}
\li{\strong{Footprint} (X1's to-do 1): \code{\verb~|Eval.Ext.bytes()~} = \code{\verb~|8 * once.length + 4 * (hashes in the log)~} once a key was entered, 0 before: the session cap sees the filter, and a session without the switch has the footprint it had.}
\li{\strong{Counters} (X1's to-do 2): \code{\verb~|Eval.Ext implements Machine.Counters~}: \code{\verb~|machine.once.first~}, \code{\verb~|machine.once.seen~} in the statistics file, reported only by sessions that asked the filter (a run without the switch writes the statistics it wrote).}
\li{\strong{A defect of the filter as X1 wrote it, found by the gate and fixed: it depended on the host depth bound.} A judgment that is spilled at its entry (\code{\verb~|d > hostDepth~}) is entered again by the driver through \code{\verb~|Eval.resume~}, which called \code{\verb~|eval~} / \code{\verb~|evalInAt~} and so \code{\verb~|table~} a second time: the filter found the key it had entered a moment before and tabled the node at its FIRST evaluation. Under D0 that is every nested node, under D128 the 0.1 - 10 \% of the judgments that spill. Convention equivalence of M8's gate with the filter as written (quick form, \code{\verb~|default,once~}, \code{\verb~|work/o1/root~\verb~|/work/status/machine-gate-quick-conv-once-nofix-tree.md~}): \strong{D0 against D128 different on 57 of 195 declarations of the tutorial, 1,008 of 1,147 of bugs, 7,894 of 8,064 of the Cedar slice; unbounded against D128 on 18 of the Cedar slice} (ticks, record words). The fix (\code{\verb~|Eval.java~}): the filter is asked exactly once per judgment, at its first entry. A first visit that is spilled is resumed without a record (\code{\verb~|EVAL[NB]~}; an inert-nest node carries \code{\verb!!|~u!!} in \code{\verb~|EVAL[IN]~}); a tabled node that is spilled is resumed by \code{\verb~|evalAgain~} / \code{\verb~|tableAgain~}, which find its record without the filter (so does the frame \code{\verb~|evalAt~} writes for FORCE). With the switch off every path is the old one. After the fix: 0 different (section 3). \code{\verb~|M2EquivTest.theSameObservablesUnderEveryDepthBoundWithTheEconomySwitches~} now also runs \code{\verb~|once~}, \code{\verb~|gated,once~}, \code{\verb~|gated,m2a,once~} (ids, ticks, trace, records, runs under D = 0, 1, 7, unbounded against 128) and fails on the filter as written.}
\li{Tests: \code{\verb~|M2EconomyTest.aKeyIsTabledFromItsSecondEvaluationOn~} (first evaluation no record, second tabled, third answered by \code{\verb~|VAL~} for one tick; reset; strict mode; three depth bounds) and \code{\verb~|aNestIsWalkedALinearNumberOfTimesWhenKeysAreTabledAtTheirSecondEvaluation~} (the 300-level dependent nest: verdicts as the reference engine's, at most twice the ticks, alone and behind the gate); \code{\verb~|M6FacadeTest~} (the name); \code{\verb~|SHostileSlowTest~} (+7 switch sets, +8 on the tree of 22:42Z; +2 in the strict test). Fast group of the patched tree: 414 tests, 0 failures, 3 skipped (published: 412); on the tree of 22:42Z 417 (published: 415).}
}

\p{The rebase is faithful to X1's build: on X1's base \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} it gives reachability +0.4 \% ticks / -37.7 \% records (X1: +0.4 \% / -37.6 \%) and the Cedar slice +5.3 \% / -15.5 \% (X1: +5.3 \% / -15.6 \%).}
}

