\p{Reading. On reachability the case-tree blocks and \code{\verb~|bodies~} took the tabling records from 8.13 M to 98.8 K; the filter removes nine tenths of the rest, which is 2 \% of the records. On the INFER-driven corpora 5 - 13 \% of the records are still tabling records and the filter removes 58 - 78 \% of them: 3 - 8 \% of all records, 6 - 21 \% of the new runs, 4 - 9 \% of the run probes - and \strong{no record probe} (-0.8 \% to +3.3 \%): a node that is evaluated a second time builds its values again, and 13 - 32 \% of the first visits do come back (7 \% on reachability). That second evaluation is the +3.0 to +5.6 \% ticks. Session resets fall by 2 - 4 \%, the bytes in use at the resets by 2 - 6 \%.}
}

