}

\p{\strong{What the gate reports for a switch that changes records and ticks by design.}}

\ul{
\li{Parts 1 and 5 (differential, pipeline) compare verdicts: the switch shows only in the tick column (Init 39.45 M -> 40.77 M, Std 64.47 M -> 66.77 M).}
\li{Part 2 (tier equivalence) compares the outcome and reason of every declaration, and K1 values, with the generic tier: a switch that changes memo contents and ticks is neither flagged nor bounded by it. There is no part that compares the switch set with the set without the switch; the +0.4 to +5.6 \% ticks have to be read off the counts.}
\li{Part 3 (convention equivalence) runs all three lanes WITH the switch and compares ticks, call events, the trace and every record word: it passes only if the switch itself is independent of the host depth bound. That is the part that failed on X1's filter (section 1, item 4) and it is the right test for this class of switch: \code{\verb~|gated~}'s finding M8-F1 was the same kind.}
\li{Part 4 (audits): the audit lanes run under \code{\verb~|scopeaudit,maskaudit~} and \code{\verb~|memocheck,shortcheck~}, which are exactly the debug modes under which the filter is off (X1's rule, kept). So the audits compare the default set under audit with \code{\verb~|default,once~} without audit - 0 differences - and \strong{do not audit \code{\verb~|once~} itself}: no memo check ever sees a session that the filter has shaped.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{4. Times}

\p{Every process inside a \src{bench/quiet.py} window entered through one host slot (\code{\verb~|work/o1/timing/window.sh~}, one line per window in \code{\verb~|timing/windows.log~}); one window = one or two corpora x three rounds x the two configurations, interleaved (odd rounds \code{\verb~|default~} first, even rounds \code{\verb~|default,once~} first). ONE binary for both configurations: the JVM launcher of \code{\verb~|work/o1/dist-once2~} (the jars of the shared distribution of 21:02Z with the patched machine jar \code{\verb~|aa1cd79a3f45~}), launcher VM flags (SerialGC, C2), \code{\verb~|-Xms = -Xmx~} = 4g (reachability, Cedar slice) or 6g, \code{\verb~|-Xmn1g~}; through \code{\verb~|bench/warm.sh --no-quiet --no-cold --engine machine --switches S --load pipelined~}. "Check only" = \code{\verb~|-X passes=N -X passes-mode=recheck -X passes-keep=engines~}; "whole pass" = \code{\verb~|-X passes=N~} (every pass loads, pipelined, and checks). The reading of a process is the mean wall clock of the last half of its later passes (\code{\verb~|wall_ms~} of the driver; \code{\verb~|timing/analyze.py~}, raw logs \code{\verb~|timing/logs/~}). The Mathlib row is slice B. The native rows are \code{\verb~|work/o1/dist-once2/bin/rlvm~}, the CE native image \code{\verb~|-O3~} of exactly those jars (\code{\verb~|work/o1/ni.sh~}), \code{\verb~|-Xmx4g~} / \code{\verb~|-Xmx6g~}; it gives the same ticks and records as the JVM.}

