\title{5. Deliverables}

\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|work/o1/patches/~} (\code{\verb~|README.md~} there): \strong{\code{\verb~|O1-once-M2.patch~}} (\code{\verb~|Eval.java~}, \code{\verb~|M2EconomyTest~}, \code{\verb~|M2EquivTest~}), \strong{\code{\verb~|O1-once-M6.patch~}} (\code{\verb~|Op.java~}, \code{\verb~|Debug.java~}, \code{\verb~|M6FacadeTest~}, \code{\verb~|SWITCHES.md~}), \strong{\code{\verb~|O1-once-S.patch~}} (\code{\verb~|SHostileSlowTest~}), per \code{\verb~|scripts/machine-sandbox.sh owner~}, against the main tree as copied at 22:42:39Z (jar \code{\verb~|97d17e57e51b~}): \code{\verb~|once~} is bit 28 there. \code{\verb~|patches-main2127Z/~}: the measured and gated tree (bit 27); \code{\verb~|patches-main2108Z/~}: the first tree. \code{\verb~|work/o1/mkpatches.sh~} checks that base + patches = the patched tree.}
\li{This report; \code{\verb~|work/o1/README.md~} (what is where); the gate pages under \code{\verb~|work/o1/root~\verb~|/work/status/~}; the counts (\code{\verb~|work/o1/counts/~}), the timing logs (\code{\verb~|work/o1/timing/~}).}
\li{One line on the board (\code{\verb~|work/status/requests.log~}).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{6. Not established}

\ul{
\li{\strong{One worker on Std, full cedar and the Mathlib slice; whole pipelined passes with one worker, and with 8 workers on reachability, the Cedar slice, Init and the Mathlib slice.} The windows were dropped when the 8-worker rows had settled the verdict (the quiet lock had waits of 5 - 10 minutes per window; \code{\verb~|timing/queue.dropped.txt~}).}
\li{\strong{Full mathlib.} The Mathlib row is slice B (54,076 units), three rounds. Full mathlib was only run once, untimed, to see that \code{\verb~|default,once~} accepts it in a 6 GiB heap (8 workers, exit 0, 77.7 s on loaded cores).}
\li{\strong{The native image beyond the rows above}: not on Init, cedar or a Mathlib slice. The JVM said no-go, so the task's order did not ask for it; the ticks (+3.0 to +5.6 \% on the INFER-driven corpora) are platform-independent and the native rows of the Cedar slice (+1.5 \%) and Std (+3.5 \%) agree with them.}
\li{\strong{Why the JVM with one worker loses 10 \% on reachability.} The reading above (code shape under C2) rests on the native row and on the counters; no \code{\verb~|-XX:+LogCompilation~}, no profile.}
\li{\strong{Instruction counts} (the arena's metric): not measured. Ticks are +5.5 \% on the Mathlib slices.}
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|once~} under audit.} The filter is off under \code{\verb~|scopeaudit~}, \code{\verb~|maskaudit~}, \code{\verb~|memocheck~}, \code{\verb~|shortcheck~}, \code{\verb~|sharecheck~} (X1's rule): no audit lane of the gate ever checks a memo in a session the filter has shaped. The evidence for \code{\verb~|once~} itself is the differential, convention equivalence, the hostile matrix and the unit tests.}
\li{\strong{The mutant corpora} (\code{\verb~|report.sh mutants~}) and DiffEngine on the large corpora with the switch: not run. con-leche, cslib, navier-stokes-euler: not run at all.}
\li{\strong{Other switch sets.} Counts for \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} and \code{\verb~|default,-bodies~} only; with \code{\verb~|eager~} (published 21:57Z) and \code{\verb~|convexpect~} (22:42Z) only the hostile matrix (\code{\verb~|default,eager,once~}) and the quick gate of the default set on that tree; with \code{\verb~|tele~}, \code{\verb~|facts~}, \code{\verb~|probes~} only the \code{\verb~|all,...,once~} row of the hostile matrix; with \code{\verb~|m2b~} and \code{\verb~|k2~} nothing.}
\li{\strong{Other session caps.} Counts and times ran with the launcher's default (the machine's cap of 1 MiB), the gate with its own setting (\code{\verb~|session cap 4 MiB~}); nothing else.}
\li{\strong{The filter's own to-dos} that X1 listed (a second filter level in place of the log; sharing the pass over the kept bindings with \code{\verb~|Values.suspRecordAt~}; the same filter for INFER's tabling records): not done; nothing measured here suggests they would change the sign.}
\li{\strong{The main tree kept moving} (E1 published at 21:26Z, 21:57Z, 22:12Z, 22:42Z; INT7 tests and notes at 23:22Z). Counts, full gate and times are the tree of 21:27Z; the delivered patch is rebased on the tree of 22:42Z and checked there (fast group, counter identity, hostile matrix, quick gate), not timed; it applies to the main tree of 23:22Z (\code{\verb~|patch --dry-run~}, no offset reported).}
}
}
